  "question": {
    "text": "The pair from the following pairs having both compounds with net non-zero dipole moment is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PL4SK",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>-Dichlorobenzene, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>-Dichlorobenzene",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Pljh5",
      "text": "cis-butene, trans-butene",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vqyHH",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HbmVl",
      "text": "Benzene, anisidine",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The dipole moment is the vector sum of all the bond moments. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> both have net non-zero dipole moment because&nbsp;the bond moments are not cancelled each other due to their tetrahedral structure. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>-dichlorobenzene, trans-butene, benzene have zero dipole moment due to&nbsp;cancellation of bond moments. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>-dichlorobenzene, cis-butene, anisidine has non-zero dipole moment.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
